  "body": "Reported: the log-workout day list didn't agree with the circular picker.\n\nTwo separate causes.\n\n**1. The picker was missing a day.** It filtered out the current day, on the\nreasoning that the \"Use Next\" card above it already covers today. That left 11\nof 12 entries, so every item below today's slot sat one position off from its\nday number — the list no longer lined up with the dial's twelve.\n\nIt now lists all 12 in cycle order as `Day 5 · Compound: Pulls`, with `(today)`\nmarking the current one. Standard rule: annotate, don't remove — dropping an\nitem from an ordered set the user already has a spatial model of silently shifts\neverything after it.\n\nThe default also moves from \"first day that isn't today\" to the current day, so\nflipping the toggle doesn't change what the card below is showing. That fixes a\nlatent bug too: the old default was computed once at mount from a `currentDay`\nthat arrives asynchronously, so it could be stale.\n\n**2. The dial spoke a different vocabulary.** It rendered `DAY_DESIGN.group`, a\nshort muscle-label list used in exactly one place, while every other surface\nrenders `DAY_CONFIG.name`:\n\n| Day | Everywhere else | Dial (before) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Compound: Legs | QUADS |\n| 3 | Hamstrings | POST. CHAIN |\n| 5 | Compound: Pulls | BACK |\n| 7 | Torso | TRAPS |\n| 8 | Pecs (Mobility) | PECS |\n| 9 | Compound: Push | PECS |\n| 12 | Grip | FOREARM |\n\nOnly days 2 and 10 matched exactly, and 8 and 9 were indistinguishable — the one\ndistinction the cycle most needs visible, since dips belong on 9 and never on 8.\n\nThe dial now renders `DAY_CONFIG.name`; `group` and `dayGroup()` are deleted.\nLong names drop 9px → 8px: \"COMPOUND: PULLS\" measures 87.1 units at 9px against\n~90 units of clear space inside the ring, which fit but would have kissed the\nring edge.\n\n## Verification\n\n`npm run build` clean. Checked in the running app with `currentDay = 5`: the\npicker's options read Day 1 through Day 12 in order with `(today)` on day 5 and\nthe select's value at 5, and the dial caption reads COMPOUND: PULLS, measured at\n77.4 units — inside the hole, no overlap.\n\nNot addressed here: the drawer's day title renders red for every day, because\n`index.css` remaps `.text-cyan-300` to `--muscle-red` while the dial uses each\nday's own accent. Separate fix.",
